# eprfs-peer

Born strict (RS-GOV-03): every lint suppression in this subtree carries a literal reason, and
the native style gate holds it at zero findings. The crate depends on `elohim-epr-rea` for the
roster, on iroh `=0.92` (with the workspace's vendored `iroh-quinn-proto` patch, as
elohim-storage carries) for the endpoint, and on `eprfs-core`/`eprfs-serve` for the tier it serves
on `/elohim/eprfs-tier/1.0.0` (`TierEndpoint` behind `StewardDevicesGate`; frames are the same
`serde_ipld_dagcbor` codec eprfs-core encodes trees with). It takes no dependency on `epr-cli`: the did:key
verifier arrives as a `&dyn SignatureVerifier` parameter. elohim-storage takes no dependency on
this crate (R-E3).

The secret key never leaves `PeerKey` except into the endpoint builder: no `Display`, `Clone`
or serialization, and `Debug` prints the node id only.
